Package: naxp
Title: Encoded ASCII Expressions
Version: 0.0.0.9000
Authors@R:
    person("Tim", "Gordon", , "tim.gordon@btinternet.com", role = c("aut", "cre"),
           comment = c(ORCID = "0009-0006-3087-4384"))
Description: Converts alphanumeric codes such as postcodes to whole numbers
    and back again, following the 'naxp' standard
    <https://naxp.org/spec/>.
    A naxp ('encoded ASCII expression') is a pattern,
    defined using a similar syntax to regular expressions,
    that maps each text it accepts to a number
    from 1 to a fixed maximum, and
    any other text to 0.
    The same pattern maps text to numbers identically across
    all 'naxp' libraries in all languages on all platforms
    (subject only to the availability of types
    able to store large enough integers).
    Standard naxps are defined for common code systems and
    are built into all 'naxp' libraries.
    Two naxps can be compared to determine, among other things, whether
    stored values keep their meaning when one replaces the other.
    Wraps the 'naxp' 'C++' library
    <https://naxp.org/api/#cpp>.
